PATH MAPPING (templated prompt path -> real XcodeGen layout)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The prompt's `apps/apple/TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/DestinationETAWidget.*`
is a generic template path. This repo's Apple app is an XcodeGen project whose
single shared SwiftUI source root is `apps/apple/Sources/` (consumed by BOTH the
iOS `TeslaSync` and macOS `TeslaSync-macOS` targets per project.yml), and whose
unit tests live under `apps/apple/Tests/Unit/`. The surface is therefore shipped
as (one component per file, per the engineering guideline + SwiftLint
file_length<=400):

  apps/apple/Sources/Dashboard/Widgets/DestinationETAWidget.swift       (view + registry + previews)
  apps/apple/Sources/Dashboard/Widgets/DestinationETAWidgetData.swift   (projection + view-state + freshness)
  apps/apple/Sources/Dashboard/Widgets/DestinationETAWidgetModel.swift  (diagnostics + live binding + model)
  apps/apple/Sources/Dashboard/Widgets/DestinationETAWidgetViews.swift  (shell + content subviews)
  apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Dashboard/DestinationETAWidgetTests.swift       (adapter + state + a11y + render tests)

These fall under the existing `Sources` / `Tests/Unit` target source roots, so
no project.yml change is required (auto-included on `xcodegen generate`).

i18n: all 10 source strings already exist in the P1/S10 catalog
(apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings) as
`translation.widget.destinationETA.{title,home,work,favorite,other,noData,min,
eta,noNav,remaining}` — no catalog edit needed. Freshness chrome uses the
existing `widget.freshness.{stale,offline,live}` and `translation.common.refresh`.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY (web DestinationETAWidget.tsx -> native)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data sources:
  useVehicles            -> Shared VehiclesStore.vehicles()              [first-vehicle fallback]
  useLocationSnapshotLatest -> Shared VehiclesStore.locationSnapshotLatest(vehicleId)
  useUnits               -> Units facade (SI -> display at render boundary)
  useTranslation         -> SwiftUI LocalizedStringKey + .xcstrings catalog
Shared components:
  @/components/feedback  -> TSEmptyState, TSQueryError, TSSkeleton
  @/components/ui        -> TSBadge (Badge), shell chrome
  @/components/data-display -> TSAnimatedNumber (AnimatedNumber), TSMetricBar
States reproduced (every one renders — no hidden surfaces):
  loading  -> skeleton chrome (TSSkeleton)
  empty    -> "No location data" (web !snapshot)               [translation.widget.destinationETA.noData]
  error    -> TSQueryError + retry (web QueryError branch)
  stale    -> stale chip + auto-refresh on rising edge
  offline  -> cached value kept on screen + offline chip / offline empty+retry
  navigating (standard) -> destination row + ETA countdown (AnimatedNumber +
                           "1h 5m"/"5m") + distance (SI->unit, 1 dp) + progress bar
  idle (standard)       -> emoji + location badge + "No active navigation"
  compact (1x2)         -> countdown big-number / location badge / empty
SI correctness: `miles_to_arrival` is read as SI meters (the web feeds it to
  convertDistanceFromSI), stored as `metersToArrival`, converted at the render
  boundary via Units.convertDistance — no _mi/_mph fields introduced.
Registry: id=destination-eta, category=maps, default 2x2, min 1x2, max 3x40
  (matches web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/registry/maps.ts).
Diagnostics: model emits `view.opened` (surface slug "DestinationETAWidget") once
  per appearance via the DestinationETADiagnostics seam; the Shared adapter maps it
  onto the P1/S11 typed taxonomy Telemetry.track(TelemetryEvent.ScreenView).

