------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENVIRONMENTAL CAVEATS (shared multi-slot runner — NOT defects in this surface)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Full-scheme iOS `test` aggregate (`build test`, which also runs the entire
  pre-existing TeslaSyncTests suite + TeslaSyncUITests) is intermittently
  disrupted by CoreSimulator/simctl contention: this runner hosts multiple
  parallel task slots that flip the shared `xcode-select` / launchd
  `DEVELOPER_DIR` and the per-user CoreSimulatorService between Command Line
  Tools and Xcode. Symptom: `xcrun: error: unable to find utility "simctl"`
  raised by the simulator coordinator even while `xcode-select -p` reports
  Xcode; tests begin executing then the simulator connection drops mid-run.
  Evidence that this is environmental and not surface-related: the SAME build +
  the SAME launchctl/DEVELOPER_DIR setup ran this surface's 21 tests fully green
  (item [5]) in a stable window. Mitigation used: DEVELOPER_DIR override +
  `launchctl setenv DEVELOPER_DIR` + simulator pre-boot + retry.
- macOS `test`: `build-for-testing` fails at the planning stage with "Could not
  find test host for TeslaSync-macOSTests" (TEST_HOST resolution) before any
  Swift is compiled. Root cause (pre-existing, NOT this surface): the macOS app
  target sets `PRODUCT_NAME: TeslaSync` (project.yml) so its product bundle is
  `TeslaSync.app` (executable `TeslaSync`), but the auto-derived test TEST_HOST
  points at `TeslaSync-macOS.app/Contents/MacOS/TeslaSync-macOS` (the target
  name) — a bundle that is never produced. Confirmed via `-showBuildSettings`
  (EXECUTABLE_PATH = TeslaSync.app/Contents/MacOS/TeslaSync, PRODUCT_NAME =
  TeslaSync). Fixing it is a shared-infra project.yml change outside this
  surface's allowed file set; the macOS app target itself builds green (item [6]),
  and this surface's logic is fully exercised by the iOS unit run (item [5]).
  Tracked alongside apps/macos-pending-verifications.md (ADR-012 CI matrix runs
  macOS verifications on macos-latest runners).

